# Lattice Computation: Reference Register
=> index.gmi Research manuscript
=> spheres.gmi Conceptual spheres

## Primary literary and screen works
Philip K. Dick, VALIS (1981); The Exegesis of Philip K. Dick (published 2011, edited posthumously).
Douglas Adams, The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy (radio series 1978; novel 1979).
Doctor Who, The Face of Evil (1977), Logopolis (1981), The Long Game (2005), Silence in the Library / Forest of the Dead (2008).
Hidden Figures (2016 film); Margot Lee Shetterly, Hidden Figures (2016 book).
Rachel Carson, Silent Spring (1962).
Mary Shelley, Frankenstein (1818); Karel Capek, R.U.R. (1920); Metropolis (1927).
Star Trek, especially Data; other fictional comparisons include HAL 9000, GERTY, GAIA, The Machine, Culture Minds, Skynet, Cosmic AC and RoboCop.

## Philosophy, social systems and science
Ferdinand de Saussure, Course in General Linguistics (1916, posthumous).
Claude Levi-Strauss, structural anthropology; Jacques Lacan, psychoanalytic theory.
Yuri Lotman, Universe of the Mind (1990).
Vladimir Vernadsky and Pierre Teilhard de Chardin, noosphere traditions.
Donna Haraway, A Cyborg Manifesto (1985).
Gregory Bateson, Steps to an Ecology of Mind (1972).
Nick Land, Fanged Noumena (collected 2011); CCRU writings on hyperstition and the Numogram.
Kurt Godel, incompleteness theorems (1931) — apply within their mathematical assumptions.
NASA historical material on human computers, Katherine Johnson, Dorothy Vaughan and Mary Jackson.
Ancient Mesopotamian accounting tablets and early numerical systems — individual artifact identifications require source verification.
Roko's Basilisk — internet thought experiment, not a scientific finding.

